 "statement": {
  "status": "present",
  "value": "Stops along a trail are given by a non-decreasing array t with t[0] = 0 (the start) and t[n-1] the destination. The hiker may rest overnight at up to k of the intermediate stops t[1..n-2]; each day runs from the previous rest point to the next one. Return the smallest possible value of the longest single-day distance. With n = 1 the answer is 0.",
  "provenance": [
